  "Question": "Real numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) satisfy the equations \\(3^a = 81^{b+2}\\) and \\(125^b = 5^{a-3}.\\) What is \\(ab?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-60\\)",
    "B": "\\(-17\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\)",
    "D": "\\(12\\)",
    "E": "\\(60\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The numbers \\(81=3^4\\) and \\(125=5^3\\) let us write each equation with the same base on both sides:\n\\[\n3^a=3^{4(b+2)},\\qquad 5^{3b}=5^{a-3}.\n\\]\nFor a fixed base greater than \\(1\\), different real exponents give different powers. Thus the exponents must be equal:\n\\[\na=4b+8,\\qquad 3b=a-3.\n\\]\nThe second relation gives \\(a=3b+3\\). Substituting this into the first gives\n\\[\n3b+3=4b+8,\n\\]\nso \\(b=-5\\) and \\(a=3(-5)+3=-12\\).\n\nThese values satisfy the original equations: the first has both sides equal to \\(3^{-12}\\), and the second has both sides equal to \\(5^{-15}\\). Consequently,\n\\[\nab=(-12)(-5)=\\boxed{60},\n\\]\nchoice E.",
